{
  "schema": "swbpipe.hanger_sizing_reference.preload/1",
  "basis": "Independent reference for the variable spring preload (DEL-04-03 REQ-014 and AC-009; DEL-04-11 REQ-014 and AC-014). A variable spring hanger is a spring of its rate k on UZ plus its cold load F_cold as a constant force along +Z, acting in every load case. It carries F_cold - k (u - g), where u is the node's UZ displacement from the drawn geometry and g the displacement of the spring's base along its axis (zero unless stated); that is its published support force. A held spring (a test case whose test condition is springs_and_constant_effort) is a rigid UZ restraint at zero displacement, and neither its stiffness nor its cold load acts; its published force is the restraint's reaction. Straight horizontal Euler-Bernoulli beams along +X with axial deformation, shear neglected, small displacements, one circular tube section: d = D - 2t, A = pi (D^2 - d^2)/4, I = pi (D^4 - d^4)/64. Z is vertical, positive up; SI units (m, N, Pa, N/m). Every load is a stored nodal force along Z; no self-weight, contents weight or line load is generated. Every published force is the force the support exerts on the pipe, positive along +Z. Values containing E I contain pi; they are computed exactly at rational lower and upper bounds of pi (Machin's formula, 120 digits) and emitted rounded to the nearest binary64, which agrees at both bounds and when every input is replaced by its binary64. Each closed form agrees exactly with an exact-rational stiffness solve. Every value is invented. See README.md for the derivations.",
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "P-A",
      "description": "Span with one spring hanger. Nodes N1..N5 at x = 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 m; members M1..M4; S-1 (N1) and S-5 (N5) rigid UZ; G-1 (N1: UX, UY, RX) and G-5 (N5: UY) restrain the out-of-plane and axial motion, UX at N1 only. Spring hanger SH-3 at N3 (UZ): k = 150000 N/m, cold load 6000 N. Stored loads F-A -5000 N at N2, F-B -7000 N at N4, F-C -3000 N at N4, F-H1 -4000 N at N2 and F-H2 -4000 N at N4 (test water). Closed form: simply supported 8 m span, f(x, a) = b x (L^2 - b^2 - x^2) / (6 E I L) with b = L - a and x <= a (symmetric); u_3 = (sum_j f(4, x_j) F_j + f(4, 4)(F_cold + k g)) / (1 + k f(4, 4)); spring force F_cold - k (u_3 - g); end reactions by statics. Held: two 4 m spans, three-moment M_B = -3 L (P1 + P2)/32, R_S1 = R_S5 = P/2 + M_B/L, R_SH3 = (P1 + P2)/2 - 2 M_B/L, with P1 and P2 the downward loads at N2 and N4.",
